## Entry points

| Import                           | Exports                                                                                                   | Needs                                                 |
| -------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |
| `@quami/sendo`                   | `createSendo`, types, errors, `metaDirect`, `agentTool`, utilities, `runDoctor` / `addAccount`            | `zod` 4, `ai` 6 (peers)                               |
| `@quami/sendo/adapters/supabase` | `supabaseAdapter`                                                                                         | `@supabase/supabase-js`                               |
| `@quami/sendo/adapters/memory`   | `memoryAdapter`                                                                                           | —                                                     |
| `@quami/sendo/adapters/drizzle`  | [`drizzleAdapter`, `DrizzleAdapterError`](https://sendo.dev/docs/adapters#drizzle)                                         | `drizzle-orm`                                         |
| `@quami/sendo/adapters/prisma`   | [`prismaAdapter`, `PrismaAdapterError`](https://sendo.dev/docs/adapters#prisma)                                            | `@prisma/client`                                      |
| `@quami/sendo/adapters/contract` | `runAdapterContract`, `runMediaStoreContract`                                                             | `vitest`                                              |
| `@quami/sendo/storage/supabase`  | [`supabaseStorage`](#media-store)                                                                         | `@supabase/supabase-js`                               |
| `@quami/sendo/storage/s3`        | [`s3Storage`, `S3StorageError`](#media-store)                                                             | `@aws-sdk/client-s3`, `@aws-sdk/s3-request-presigner` |
| `@quami/sendo/snippets`          | Client-safe snippet helpers: `searchSnippets`, `findSnippetVariables`, `fillSnippetVariables`, limits     | —                                                     |
| `@quami/sendo/rules`             | Client-safe rule schemas: `ruleParamsSchemas`, `ruleKeySchema`, `WEEKDAYS`, `parseRuleParams`, rule types | `zod` 4                                               |
| `@quami/sendo/next`              | `toNextHandlers`                                                                                          | `next`                                                |
| `npx @quami/sendo`               | [doctor, accounts add](https://sendo.dev/docs/cli)                                                                         | —                                                     |

Everything runs on the server with the Supabase service role. Never import `lib/sendo.ts` from a client component. Client components may import values only from `@quami/sendo/snippets` and `@quami/sendo/rules` (`import type` from `@quami/sendo` is fine): the main entry pulls the server runtime (`ai`, `node:crypto`) into the browser bundle.

## createSendo config

```ts title="lib/sendo.ts"
import { createSendo } from "@quami/sendo";
import { supabaseAdapter } from "@quami/sendo/adapters/supabase";
import { createClient } from "@supabase/supabase-js";
import { z } from "zod";

function requireEnv(name: string): string {
  const value = process.env[name];
  if (value === undefined || value.trim() === "") {
    throw new Error(`[sendo] Missing environment variable ${name}. Add it to .env.local.`);
  }
  return value;
}

// Service-role client: server only, never import this file from client components.
const supabaseAdmin = createClient(
  requireEnv("NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL"),
  requireEnv("SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY"),
  { auth: { persistSession: false, autoRefreshToken: false } },
);

export const sendo = createSendo({
  adapter: supabaseAdapter(supabaseAdmin, {
    storageBucket: process.env.SENDO_STORAGE_BUCKET ?? "sendo-media",
  }),
  appSecret: requireEnv("SENDO_META_APP_SECRET"),
  verifyToken: requireEnv("SENDO_VERIFY_TOKEN"),
  // sendo_accounts.token_ref holds the NAME of the env var with the token (e.g. SENDO_TOKEN_MAIN).
  resolveToken: (account) => process.env[account.tokenRef],
  // findPatientIdByPhone / listAdminIds stand for your own queries.
  // Your entity id for this phone number (patient, resident, user), or null.
  linkContact: async ({ phone, account }) => findPatientIdByPhone(phone, account.tenantId),
  // Who gets a handed-off conversation. Exactly one id auto-assigns it.
  resolveHandoffTargets: async ({ account }) => listAdminIds(account.tenantId),
  agentDefaults: { historyLimit: 20, maxStepsPerTurn: 5, maxMessagesPerMinutePerContact: 10 },
  eventRetentionDays: 30,
  logger: console,
});
```

| Option                    | Type                                                                | Default / notes                                                                                 |
| ------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `adapter`                 | `SendoAdapter`                                                      | Required. supabaseAdapter or memoryAdapter.                                                     |
| `media`                   | `MediaStore`                                                        | Where media bytes live ([MediaStore](#media-store)). Default: the adapter's storage.            |
| `appSecret`               | `string`                                                            | Required unless transport or connect is set. Verifies X-Hub-Signature-256.                      |
| `verifyToken`             | `string`                                                            | Required unless transport is set. Webhook GET challenge.                                        |
| `resolveToken`            | `(account) => string \| null \| undefined \| Promise<…>`            | Required unless transport is set. Called per Meta call; empty → ConfigError.                    |
| `transport`               | `Transport`                                                         | Replaces the three options above (metaDirect(...) or your own Transport).                       |
| `graphVersion`            | `string`                                                            | GRAPH_API_VERSION ("v26.0"). Shorthand config only.                                             |
| `fetch`                   | `typeof fetch`                                                      | globalThis.fetch. Shorthand config only.                                                        |
| `linkContact`             | `({ phone, account, contact }) => string \| null`                   | Called on a new contact and when the profile name changes; stored in contact.appRef.            |
| `resolveHandoffTargets`   | `({ to, account, conversation, contact }) => string[]`              | Handoff assignees. Exactly one id sets assignedTo.                                              |
| `agentDefaults`           | `{ historyLimit, maxStepsPerTurn, maxMessagesPerMinutePerContact }` | 20, 5, 10                                                                                       |
| `eventRetentionDays`      | `number`                                                            | 30 (sendo.maintenance.prune)                                                                    |
| `locale`                  | `"en" \| "es"`                                                      | "en". Language of the built-in handoff and opt-out messages (BUILT_IN_MESSAGES[locale]).        |
| `handoffMessage`          | `string \| null`                                                    | BUILT_IN_MESSAGES[locale].handoff ("Connecting you with someone from the team."); null: none.   |
| `defaultCountry`          | `string`                                                            | ISO-2 or calling code for national numbers, e.g. "GT".                                          |
| `logger`                  | `Logger`                                                            | Console-like. Every line is redacted (tokens, secrets, Authorization).                          |
| `storeToken`              | `({ account, token }) => Promise<string>`                           | Embedded Signup token storage; returns the tokenRef.                                            |
| `deleteToken`             | `(tokenRef) => Promise<void>`                                       | Called by sendo.accounts.disconnect.                                                            |
| `meta`                    | `{ appId?, configId? }`                                             | Your Meta app, for Embedded Signup.                                                             |
| `coexistence`             | `{ pauseAgentOnPhoneReply?, importHistory? }`                       | true, false. Numbers shared with the WhatsApp Business app.                                     |
| `connect`                 | `{ apiKey, signingSecret, baseUrl? }`                               | Sendo Connect: relay signature and signup ([Sendo Connect](https://sendo.dev/docs/sendo-connect)).               |
| `optOut`                  | `{ keywords?, confirmation? }`                                      | ["BAJA","STOP","ALTO","CANCELAR"], BUILT_IN_MESSAGES[locale].optOutConfirmation; null: none.    |
| `transcribe`              | `{ model, timeoutMs? }`                                             | AI SDK transcription model for inbound voice notes ([Voice notes](https://sendo.dev/docs/voice-notes-and-cost)). |
| `resolveRole`             | `({ userId, tenantId }) => { role, queues? } \| null`               | Required for `sendo.actor` and every `{ actor }` API; null means no access.                     |
| `resolveUsers`            | `(ids) => { id, name, avatarUrl? }[]`                               | Names and avatars in the inbox and metrics.                                                     |
| `resolveAssignees`        | `({ tenantId, queue, account }) => string[]`                        | Assign menu and `auto_assign` rules. Falls back to `resolveHandoffTargets`.                     |
| `resolveSnippetVariables` | `({ contact, conversation, account }) => Record<string, string>`    | App variables for `snippets.render` (e.g. `saldo`).                                             |

`createSendo` throws `ConfigError` on invalid config. On first use it checks `sendo_schema_meta` and logs a warning when the tables are missing or older than `SENDO_SCHEMA_VERSION`.

## Events (sendo.on)

`sendo.on(event, handler)` returns an unsubscribe function. Handlers run one after another in the background pipeline; a throwing handler is logged and the pipeline goes on.

| Event                  | Payload                                                    | When                                                                                                  |
| ---------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `message`              | `{ message, contact, conversation, account, reply }`       | Each new inbound message, after it (and its media) is stored. message.media is the Media row or null. |
| `status`               | `{ message, status, error? }`                              | A delivery status moved an outbound message forward (sent → delivered → read, or failed).             |
| `handoff`              | `{ conversation, contact, account, reason, assignees }`    | A conversation was handed to humans.                                                                  |
| `conversation.status`  | `{ conversation, from, to, by }`                           | agent / human / closed changes, including a reopen (by "system").                                     |
| `account.error`        | `{ account, error }`                                       | Meta rejected the account token (error.isInvalidToken, code 190).                                     |
| `account.default`      | `{ tenantId, account, previous }`                          | A tenant's default number changed (account is null when it has none).                                 |
| `account.disconnected` | `{ account, by }`                                          | sendo.accounts.disconnect.                                                                            |
| `account.billing`      | `{ account, billingReady, previous }`                      | A number's payment-method state changed.                                                              |
| `event.unrouted`       | `{ phoneNumberId, raw }`                                   | A webhook for a phone_number_id with no active sendo_accounts row.                                    |
| `contact.opt_in`       | `{ contact, optIn, previous, source, keyword, messageId }` | sendo.contacts.setOptIn or an inbound opt-out keyword changed a contact's marketing opt-in.           |

```ts title="ts"
const unsubscribe = sendo.on("message", async ({ message, contact, conversation, reply }) => {
  if (message.type === "text" && message.text?.trim().toLowerCase() === "menu") {
    await reply.buttons({
      body: `Hola ${contact.profileName ?? ""}, ¿qué necesitas?`,
      buttons: [
        { id: "cita", title: "Agendar cita" },
        { id: "humano", title: "Hablar con alguien" },
      ],
    });
  }
  if (message.media?.downloadStatus === "done") {
    console.log("stored at", message.media.storagePath, "in", conversation.id);
  }
});

sendo.on("status", ({ message, status, error }) => {
  if (status === "failed") console.warn("send failed", message.id, error?.code, error?.message);
});

sendo.on("handoff", async ({ conversation, assignees, reason }) => {
  await notifyStaff(assignees, `Conversación ${conversation.id}: ${reason}`);
});

sendo.on("conversation.status", ({ conversation, from, to, by }) => {
  console.log(conversation.id, from, "→", to, "by", by);
});

sendo.on("account.error", ({ account, error }) => {
  if (error.isInvalidToken) console.error(`Token ${account.tokenRef} expired or was revoked`);
});

sendo.on("event.unrouted", ({ phoneNumberId }) => {
  console.warn("Webhook for an unknown phone_number_id", phoneNumberId);
});

unsubscribe(); // stop listening
```

## Sending (sendo.send)

```ts title="signatures"
sendo.send.text(to, body, { account?, tenant?, previewUrl?, replyTo? }): Promise<Message>
sendo.send.media(to, { type, url? | file? | id?, mimeType?, caption?, filename? }, { account?, tenant?, replyTo? })
sendo.send.buttons(to, { body, buttons: { id, title }[] /* ≤ 3 */, header?, footer? }, { account?, tenant?, replyTo? })
sendo.send.list(to, { body, button, sections, header?, footer? }, { account?, tenant?, replyTo? })
sendo.send.template(to, name, { language, variables?, headerMedia?, buttons?, account?, tenant?, replyTo? })
sendo.send.markRead(messageId): Promise<void>
```

Every send:

1. normalizes the number to E.164 (`InvalidPhoneError`);
2. resolves the account: the `account` option, else the `tenant`'s default (or only) number, else the only active account; `AmbiguousAccountError` when that is not one number ([resolution order](https://sendo.dev/docs/numbers-and-tenants#resolution));
3. gets or creates the contact and the conversation;
4. checks the 24-hour window, except for templates (`WindowClosedError`, before any write or Meta call);
5. inserts a `sendo_messages` row with status `pending` (sender `system`);
6. calls Meta (file media is uploaded first);
7. stores the Meta id and status `sent`, or `failed` with the error and rethrows.

```ts title="ts"
// Numbers are normalized to E.164: "+502 5555-1234" and "50255551234" both work.
const message = await sendo.send.text("+502 5555-1234", "Hola, tu cita está confirmada.", {
  previewUrl: false,
});
console.log(message.id, message.metaMessageId, message.status); // "sent"

await sendo.send.media("50255551234", { type: "image", url: "https://example.com/receta.png" });
await sendo.send.media("50255551234", { type: "document", file, filename: "factura.pdf" });

await sendo.send.buttons("50255551234", {
  body: "¿Confirmas tu cita de mañana a las 10:00?",
  buttons: [
    { id: "confirmar", title: "Confirmar" },
    { id: "reprogramar", title: "Reprogramar" },
  ],
  footer: "Clínica Central",
});

await sendo.send.list("50255551234", {
  body: "Elige un servicio",
  button: "Ver servicios",
  sections: [
    {
      title: "Consultas",
      rows: [
        { id: "general", title: "Medicina general" },
        { id: "pediatria", title: "Pediatría", description: "Lunes a viernes" },
      ],
    },
  ],
});

// Templates work outside the 24-hour window. Positional {{1}} or named {{nombre}} variables.
await sendo.send.template("50255551234", "recordatorio_cita", {
  language: "es",
  variables: ["Ana", "mañana 10:00"],
});

await sendo.send.markRead("wamid.HBgLNTAy..."); // sendo id or Meta id of an inbound message
```

> **Note:**
>
> Templates are read from `sendo_templates`, not from Meta: call `sendo.templates.sync()` after creating or editing templates, or `send.template` throws `TemplateNotFoundError`. A wrong number of variables throws `TemplateVariablesError`. Media is checked against Meta’s limits (image 5 MB, audio/video 16 MB, document 100 MB, sticker 500 KB) before upload.

## reply

The `reply` in the `message` event is bound to the conversation and stores sends with that sender: `text(body, opts?)`, `media(media, opts?)`, `buttons(input, opts?)`, `list(input, opts?)`, `template(name, opts)`, `react(emoji, messageId?)` (`""` removes the reaction) and `markRead(messageId?)`. Both default to the inbound message.

## sendo.templates

```ts title="ts"
// Pull approved templates from Meta into sendo_templates (run after creating or editing one).
await sendo.templates.sync(); // every active account, or { account }
const templates = await sendo.templates.list({ status: "APPROVED" });
console.log(templates.map((t) => `${t.name}/${t.language} (${t.variableCount} vars)`));
```

- `sync({ account?, tenant? })` pulls templates from Meta (one account, the tenant's active accounts, or every active account), upserts them and marks the ones deleted on Meta inactive. Returns `Template[]`.
- `list({ account?, tenant?, status?, includeInactive? })` reads `sendo_templates`.

## sendo.accounts

`list`, `get`, `add`, `setDefault`, `setLabel`, `pauseAgent`, `setAgentMode`, `disconnect`, `purge`, `refreshBilling` and `completeEmbeddedSignup`. See [Numbers and tenants](https://sendo.dev/docs/numbers-and-tenants#accounts).

## sendo.conversations

```ts title="ts"
const conversation = await sendo.conversations.get(conversationId); // null if unknown
const { open, expiresAt } = await sendo.conversations.windowStatus(conversationId);

await sendo.conversations.handoff(conversationId, { reason: "Pide hablar con una persona" });
await sendo.conversations.assign(conversationId, userId, { by: userId }); // also sets "human"
await sendo.conversations.returnToAgent(conversationId, { by: userId });
await sendo.conversations.close(conversationId, { by: userId });
// No agent turns on this conversation; on resume it doesn't answer what arrived meanwhile.
await sendo.conversations.pauseAgent(conversationId, true, { by: userId });
```

- `handoff(id, { reason, to?, message?, by? })`: status `human`, reason stored, `resolveHandoffTargets` called (one assignee → `assignedTo`), the handoff message sent, `handoff` event emitted.
- `returnToAgent(id)` clears `assignedTo` and `handoffReason`; `close(id)` closes it. A new inbound message reopens a closed conversation with status `agent`.
- `assign(id, userId)` also moves the conversation to `human`; `assign(id, null)` only unassigns.
- `pauseAgent(id, paused, { by? })` stops (or resumes) the agent on one conversation; on resume it doesn't answer what arrived during the pause. Emits `conversation.agent_paused`.
- `by` (default `"system"`) shows up in the `conversation.status`, `conversation.assigned` and `conversation.agent_paused` events and in the thread's system line.

## sendo.inbox

Server-side operations behind the inbox server actions. Every method takes `{ actor }` from `sendo.actor(userId, tenantId)` and enforces the role matrix ([Team inbox](https://sendo.dev/docs/team-inbox#roles)): another tenant's conversation is `RecordNotFoundError`, a conversation or action the actor isn't allowed is `ForbiddenError`. A missing or forged actor (no user id, unknown or `null` role) is `ForbiddenError` with `role: null` in every `{ actor }` API, and an `accountId` filter that isn't a number of the actor's tenant is `AccountNotFoundError`.

| Method                                                                                                | Returns                   | Notes                                                                                                                  |
| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `list({ actor, status?, mine?, assignedTo?, queue?, tagIds?, accountId?, search?, cursor?, limit? })` | `Page<InboxConversation>` | Agents only get what they may see. Most recent activity first. Limit 30, max 100. `count(query)` counts them.          |
| `get(id, { actor })`                                                                                  | `InboxConversation`       | One conversation.                                                                                                      |
| `thread(id, { actor, cursor?, limit? })`                                                              | `Page<InboxMessage>`      | Newest first, notes, system lines and drafts included. Media URLs signed for 300 s. Limit 50, max 100.                 |
| `reply(id, payload, { actor })`                                                                       | `InboxMessage`            | Step-in: sender human, status unchanged, pending draft discarded. WindowClosedError outside the window.                |
| `note(id, text, { actor })`                                                                           | `InboxMessage`            | Internal note, never sent.                                                                                             |
| `take` / `returnToAgent` / `close(id, { actor })`                                                     | `InboxConversation`       | Take assigns the actor and moves to human.                                                                             |
| `assign(id, userId \| null, { actor })`                                                               | `InboxConversation`       | Anyone but the actor needs `conversations.reassign`.                                                                   |
| `pauseAgent(id, paused, { actor })`                                                                   | `InboxConversation`       | Needs `conversations.pause_agent`.                                                                                     |
| `approveDraft(messageId, { actor, text? })` / `discardDraft(messageId, { actor })`                    | `InboxMessage` / `void`   | WindowClosedError when the window closed.                                                                              |
| `markSeen(id, { actor })`                                                                             | `void`                    | Resets unreadCount.                                                                                                    |
| `assignees(id, { actor })`                                                                            | `InboxAssignee[]`         | From `resolveAssignees` and `resolveUsers`.                                                                            |
| `tags.add` / `tags.remove(id, tagId, { actor })`                                                      | `InboxTag[]`              | The conversation's tags afterwards.                                                                                    |
| `cost(id, { actor })`                                                                                 | `InboxConversationCost`   | `{ turns, tokensIn, tokensOut, costCents, unpricedTurns }` over every agent turn, drafts included. Needs `costs.view`. |

`InboxConversation` adds `window`, `contact.displayName`, `lastMessagePreview`, `channel`, `source`, `queue`, `assignee`, `handoff { reason, by, at }`, `agentPaused` / `agentPausedOn`, `hasPendingDraft`, `accountActive` and `tags`. `InboxMessage` adds `internal`, `systemLine` (`{ kind, event, by, params }`, see [System events](https://sendo.dev/docs/team-inbox#system-events)), `draft`, `handoffAfterDraft`, `approvedBy`, `edited`, `origin`, `source`, `transcription` (`{ model, ms, error }` for transcribed or failed voice notes, else `null`), and `tokensIn` / `tokensOut` / `costCents` (admins only). A disconnected number makes `reply`, `note` and `approveDraft` throw `AccountStateError` (`ACCOUNT_STATE`).

## sendo.snippets, sendo.tags and sendo.links

Every method takes `{ actor }` and is scoped to the actor's tenant.

| Method                                                                                                      | Returns                       | Notes                                                                                                 |
| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `snippets.list({ actor, accountId? })`                                                                      | `Snippet[]`                   | Team snippets plus the actor's personal ones; with `accountId`, only those usable on that number.     |
| `snippets.get(id, { actor })`                                                                               | `Snippet`                     | Someone else's personal snippet is `RecordNotFoundError`.                                             |
| `snippets.upsert({ id?, shortcut, body, visibility?, accountId? }, { actor })`                              | `Snippet`                     | Team snippets need `snippets.manage_tenant`. Taken shortcut: `ConstraintViolationError`.              |
| `snippets.delete(id, { actor })`                                                                            | `void`                        |                                                                                                       |
| `snippets.render(snippetId, { actor, conversationId })`                                                     | `{ text, unresolved }`        | Fills `{{nombre}}`, `{{telefono}}`, `{{agente}}` and `resolveSnippetVariables`; the rest stays as is. |
| `tags.list({ actor })`                                                                                      | `Tag[]`                       | Every role.                                                                                           |
| `tags.upsert({ id?, name, color }, { actor })` / `tags.delete(id, { actor })` / `tags.usage(id, { actor })` | `Tag` / `void` / `number`     | Need `tags.manage`. Deleting removes the tag from every conversation.                                 |
| `links.create({ account?, tenant?, text?, source })`                                                        | `{ url, code, phone, text }`  | A `wa.me` link whose text ends in `[#source]` (attribution). No actor needed.                         |
| `links.sources({ actor, account?, from?, to? })`                                                            | `{ source, conversations }[]` | Conversations per source; needs `numbers.manage`.                                                     |

See [Snippets and tags](https://sendo.dev/docs/team-inbox#snippets-tags) and [Widgets](https://sendo.dev/docs/widgets).

## Broadcasts and opt-in

`sendo.broadcasts` sends one APPROVED template to many contacts. Every method takes `{ actor }` and needs `broadcasts.manage` (admins); another tenant's broadcast is `RecordNotFoundError`.

- `preview({ actor, template, language, recipients, variables?, account?, ratePerMinute? })` returns `{ total, eligible, skipped: { no_opt_in, opted_out, invalid_phone }, category, ratePerMinute, estimatedMinutes }` and writes nothing.
- `create(sameInput)` stores a `queued` broadcast. Recipients are contact ids, `{ phone }` (upserted as a contact) or `{ contactId | phone, variables }`. MARKETING templates go only to contacts with `marketingOptIn = true`; UTILITY and AUTHENTICATION go to everyone who hasn't explicitly opted out. Ineligible recipients are stored `skipped` with the reason. `ratePerMinute` defaults to 60.
- `get(id)` adds `counts` per recipient status, `recipients(id, { status?, cursor?, limit? })` pages the per-recipient results, `list({ cursor?, limit? })` is newest first, and `cancel(id)` turns pending recipients into `cancelled`.
- `sendo.maintenance.tick()` sends up to `ratePerMinute` recipients per broadcast and minute. Status webhooks update each recipient. Meta 131042 pauses the broadcast (`pauseReason: "billing"`, number `billingReady = false`) until billing is ready again; a rate limit (130429) leaves recipients `pending` for the next tick. Broadcast messages never move a conversation to `human` or run the agent; replies land in the normal conversation.
- `sendo.contacts.setOptIn(contactId, optIn, { source? })` records an explicit decision (`marketingOptIn`, `optInAt = now`) and emits `contact.opt_in`. An inbound message that is exactly an `optOut` keyword (trimmed, case and accents ignored) opts the contact out, sends the confirmation inside the 24-hour window and skips the agent turn.

## sendo.metrics

Read-only reports for supervisors and admins. Every method takes `{ actor, from, to, account?, tagIds? }` (`to` is exclusive; `account` is an account id or Meta phone number id of the actor's tenant; `tagIds` cuts by any matching tag) and needs `metrics.view`. Agents get `ForbiddenError`.

| Method                         | Returns                     | Notes                                                                                                                                  |
| ------------------------------ | --------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `metrics.daily(query)`         | `MetricsDaily[]`            | Per account and local day: inbound, outbound, conversations started and closed. Cost and token fields are `null` without `costs.view`. |
| `metrics.byAssignee(query)`    | `MetricsAssignee[]`         | Conversations, messages sent and median first response per person, with `name` / `avatarUrl` from `resolveUsers`.                      |
| `metrics.firstResponse(query)` | `MetricsFirstResponseRow[]` | One row per conversation. Notes, drafts and imported messages don't count.                                                             |
| `metrics.aiResolution(query)`  | `MetricsAiResolutionRow[]`  | Closed conversations with no handoff and no human message.                                                                             |
| `metrics.bySource(query)`      | `MetricsSourceRow[]`        | Conversations per source (`[#code]`, `ad:<id>`, `null` for direct) and day.                                                            |
| `metrics.cost(query)`          | `MetricsCostRow[]`          | Cost and tokens per AI agent and day. Needs `costs.view` (admins).                                                                     |

`metricsDayRange({ from, to, timeZone })` turns local dates into the `from` / `to` instants. Drizzle and Prisma apps can run the same queries with `METRICS_SQL` and `metricsSqlParams` ([Metrics](https://sendo.dev/docs/metrics#sql)).

## sendo.events and sendo.maintenance

Every webhook POST is stored in `sendo_events` before the 200 and ends as `processed`, `failed` (with a redacted error) or `unrouted`.

```ts title="ts"
const event = await sendo.events.get(eventId); // raw payload + status
if (event?.status === "failed" || event?.status === "unrouted") {
  const after = await sendo.events.reprocess(eventId); // idempotent: messages are deduped
  console.log(after.status, after.error);
}
```

```ts title="ts"
const deleted = await sendo.maintenance.prune(); // eventRetentionDays (default 30)
await sendo.maintenance.prune({ olderThanDays: 7 });
```

Scheduling the prune: [Retention](https://sendo.dev/docs/retention).

## sendo.handleWebhook

`sendo.handleWebhook(request, { waitUntil? })` is the framework-agnostic entry point (Web `Request` → `Response`):

| Request                                            | Response                                            |
| -------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |
| GET with the matching hub.verify_token             | 200 with hub.challenge (text/plain)                 |
| GET with a wrong or missing token                  | 403                                                 |
| POST with a missing or invalid X-Hub-Signature-256 | 401, nothing stored                                 |
| POST with a body that isn't JSON                   | 400                                                 |
| POST, event could not be stored                    | 500 (Meta retries)                                  |
| POST, event stored                                 | 200 immediately; processing continues via waitUntil |
| Any other method                                   | 405                                                 |

```ts title="ts"
// Any runtime with Web Request/Response (Hono, Supabase Edge Functions, Workers...).
const worker = {
  fetch(request: Request, _env: unknown, ctx: { waitUntil(p: Promise<unknown>): void }) {
    // GET: verify challenge. POST: signature check, store event, 200, then process in
    // the background through waitUntil (without it the work runs as a detached promise).
    return sendo.handleWebhook(request, { waitUntil: (p) => ctx.waitUntil(p) });
  },
};

export default worker;
```

## @quami/sendo/next

`toNextHandlers(sendo, { waitUntil? })` returns `{ GET, POST }` for an App Router route. `POST` keeps the pipeline alive with `after()` from `next/server` (loaded lazily); pass `waitUntil` to override it.

```ts title="app/api/sendo/webhook/route.ts"
// app/api/sendo/webhook/route.ts (installed by @sendo/webhook)
import { toNextHandlers } from "@quami/sendo/next";
import { sendo } from "@/lib/sendo";

export const { GET, POST } = toNextHandlers(sendo); // POST uses next/server `after()`
export const runtime = "nodejs";
export const maxDuration = 60;
```

## Agents (sendo.agent)

`sendo.agent(definition)` registers an agent and returns `{ name, remove() }`. It answers inbound messages in conversations whose status is `agent` on the accounts it matches. Only one agent may match an account.

| Field                                                                | Notes                                                                                                                                                                |
| -------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `name`                                                               | Unique; stored as senderRef of the agent's messages.                                                                                                                 |
| `accounts?`                                                          | Account ids / phone number ids, or `(account) => boolean`. Default: all.                                                                                             |
| `tenants?`                                                           | Tenant ids (`null` = no tenant) or `(tenantId) => boolean`. ANDed with `accounts`. Default: all. See [one agent for many tenants](https://sendo.dev/docs/numbers-and-tenants#agents). |
| `mode?`                                                              | `"auto"` or `"draft"`; the number's `agentMode` wins. Default `"auto"`.                                                                                              |
| `model`                                                              | Gateway id string ("openai/gpt-5-mini") or an AI SDK LanguageModel.                                                                                                  |
| `instructions`                                                       | string or `({ account, contact, conversation, sendo }) => string \| Promise<string>`.                                                                                |
| `tools?`                                                             | `{ [name]: { description?, input: zod schema, run(ctx) } }`. Use agentTool() for typed input.                                                                        |
| `handoff?`                                                           | `{ when, to, message? }` adds the `transferir_a_humano({ motivo })` tool.                                                                                            |
| `historyLimit? / maxStepsPerTurn? / maxMessagesPerMinutePerContact?` | Default agentDefaults (20 / 5 / 10).                                                                                                                                 |
| `fallbackMessage?`                                                   | Sent when the model or a turn fails. Default: nothing.                                                                                                               |
| `vision?`                                                            | Default true: images go to the model as image parts; false describes them in text.                                                                                   |
| `timezone?`                                                          | IANA zone for the date in the system prompt. Default: the account's.                                                                                                 |
| `pricing?`                                                           | `{ inputPerMTok, outputPerMTok }` in USD, for `costCents` when the provider reports no cost. See [usage and cost](https://sendo.dev/docs/team-inbox#cost).                            |

```ts title="ts"
const agendarCita = agentTool({
  description: "Agenda una cita para el paciente vinculado a esta conversación",
  input: z.object({ fecha: z.iso.date(), hora: z.string().regex(/^\d{2}:\d{2}$/) }),
  // `input` is already validated (and typed) by the zod schema.
  async run({ input, contact, account }) {
    // Authorize inside the tool: only act on the entity linked to THIS contact.
    if (contact.appRef === null) {
      return { error: "Paciente no identificado. Pide su número de DPI." };
    }
    return bookAppointment({
      tenantId: account.tenantId,
      patientId: contact.appRef,
      date: input.fecha,
      time: input.hora,
    });
  },
});
```

```ts title="ts"
const handle = sendo.agent({
  name: "recepcion",
  // Only numbers of tenants with the feature on (or a list of account / phone number ids).
  accounts: (account) => account.tenantId !== null,
  model: "openai/gpt-5-mini",
  instructions: async ({ contact, account }) =>
    `Eres la recepción de ${await clinicName(account.tenantId)}. ` +
    `Atiende a ${contact.profileName ?? "el paciente"} en español, en mensajes breves.`,
  tools: { agendar_cita: agendarCita },
  handoff: {
    when: "pide hablar con una persona, tiene una urgencia o está molesto",
    to: "recepcion",
    message: "Te comunico con una persona del equipo.", // null sends nothing
  },
  historyLimit: 20,
  maxStepsPerTurn: 5,
  maxMessagesPerMinutePerContact: 10,
  fallbackMessage: null,
  vision: true,
  timezone: "America/Guatemala",
});

console.log(handle.name, HANDOFF_TOOL_NAME); // "recepcion", "transferir_a_humano"
handle.remove(); // unregister
```

One turn, per conversation:

1. Takes the `conv:<id>` lock (60 s); if another turn holds it, that turn picks up the new message. With the lock held, skips the turn when the conversation or its number is paused (`agentPaused`) or a rule holds the agent; the message is still stored. A pause set during a turn lets that turn finish.
2. Skips the turn when the contact sent more than `maxMessagesPerMinutePerContact` messages in the last minute (messages are still stored).
3. Builds the system prompt in English (instructions, handoff clause, an instruction to reply in the contact's language, contact name / phone / `appRef`, current date and time) and the last `historyLimit` messages of this conversation only.
4. Runs `generateText` with `stopWhen: stepCountIs(maxStepsPerTurn)`. Tool input is validated with zod before `run`; each tool receives `{ input, contact, conversation, account, sendo }`.
5. Sends the final text as sender `agent` (or stores it as a draft in draft mode) with the turn's tokens and cost; tool calls and results go to `sendo_messages.metadata`, never to the user. Notes, system lines and drafts are never part of the model's history.
6. Loops while new inbound messages arrived (at most 3 turns), then releases the lock. On errors: logs, sends `fallbackMessage` if set, never leaves the lock held.

When the model calls `transferir_a_humano`, Sendo runs `sendo.conversations.handoff` (by `agent:<name>`) and the agent stays silent until the conversation returns to `agent`.

## Adapters

All storage goes through a `SendoAdapter`. Two ship with the package; both pass the same contract suite.

### supabaseAdapter

```ts title="ts"
import { supabaseAdapter } from "@quami/sendo/adapters/supabase";
import { createClient } from "@supabase/supabase-js";

// The SERVICE ROLE client (bypasses RLS). Server only.
const supabaseAdmin = createClient(
  process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL ?? "",
  process.env.SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY ?? "",
  { auth: { persistSession: false, autoRefreshToken: false } },
);

export const adapter = supabaseAdapter(supabaseAdmin, {
  storageBucket: "sendo-media", // private bucket
  signedUrlTtlSec: 300,
});
```

Uses the service-role client, the `sendo_*` tables and RPCs from the migration, and `supabaseStorage` on the given `storageBucket` as its default [media store](#media-store) (`createSendo({ media })` overrides it). Database errors surface as `SupabaseAdapterError` (`code`, `operation`, `details`, `hint`).

### memoryAdapter

```ts title="ts"
import { createSendo } from "@quami/sendo";
import { memoryAdapter } from "@quami/sendo/adapters/memory";

// In-memory storage for unit tests and quick experiments. Nothing is persisted.
const adapter = memoryAdapter({ now: () => new Date("2026-10-06T12:00:00Z") });

const sendo = createSendo({
  adapter,
  appSecret: "test-secret",
  verifyToken: "test-verify",
  resolveToken: () => "test-token",
});

await adapter.accounts.insert({
  phoneNumberId: "100000000000001",
  wabaId: "200000000000001",
  displayPhone: "+1 555 000 1111",
  tokenRef: "SENDO_TOKEN_MAIN",
});
adapter.reset(); // clears every table between tests
```

Options: `now` (clock), `signedUrlBase`, and `schemaVersion` / `missingTables` / `bucketExists` (what `storage.exists()` returns) to simulate broken setups. Use it in unit tests with a mocked `fetch` for Meta.

### runAdapterContract

A Vitest suite every adapter must pass (accounts, contacts, conversations, messages including the forward-only status rule and the status race, media, templates, events, locks, storage, schema version). Write your own adapter and run:

```ts title="my-adapter.contract.test.ts"
// my-adapter.contract.test.ts (run with Vitest)
import { runAdapterContract } from "@quami/sendo/adapters/contract";
import type { SendoAdapter } from "@quami/sendo";

declare function createMyAdapter(): Promise<SendoAdapter>;
declare function truncateTables(): Promise<void>;
declare const databaseReachable: boolean;

runAdapterContract("my-adapter", () => createMyAdapter(), {
  skip: databaseReachable ? false : "database unreachable",
  afterEach: truncateTables,
});
```

## Media storage (MediaStore)

Inbound media (images, voice notes, documents) is downloaded from Meta and stored through a `MediaStore`. The same store signs the URLs `sendo.inbox.thread` returns (300 s), feeds images to agents with `vision`, deletes the objects on `sendo.accounts.purge`, and is what `sendo doctor` checks.

```ts
interface MediaStore {
  put(path: string, bytes: Uint8Array, mimeType: string): Promise<void>;
  get(path: string): Promise<Uint8Array | null>; // null when missing
  signedUrl(path: string, ttlSeconds: number): Promise<string>;
  delete(paths: string[]): Promise<void>; // missing paths are ignored
  exists?(): Promise<boolean>; // doctor's bucket check
}
```

Which store is used: `createSendo({ media })` if set, else the adapter's default `storage` (`supabaseAdapter` → `supabaseStorage` on its `storageBucket`; `memoryAdapter` → an in-memory map). With neither, inbound media is stored as `failed`, an error is logged and doctor fails with a `config` fix.

- **`supabaseStorage({ client, bucket, signedUrlTtlSec? })`** from `@quami/sendo/storage/supabase`: a private Supabase Storage bucket with the service-role client. It's what `supabaseAdapter` uses, so you only need it to pair Supabase Storage with another adapter.
- **`s3Storage({ client, bucket, signedUrlTtlSec? })`** from `@quami/sendo/storage/s3`: AWS S3, Cloudflare R2, MinIO and other S3-compatible stores. Install the optional peers `@aws-sdk/client-s3` and `@aws-sdk/s3-request-presigner`. Signed URLs are SigV4 presigned `GetObject` URLs (TTL capped at 7 days); deletes are batched 1000 keys per `DeleteObjects`. Failures are `S3StorageError` (`operation`, `code`, `status`). The credentials need `s3:PutObject`, `s3:GetObject`, `s3:DeleteObject` and, for doctor, `s3:ListBucket` (HeadBucket).

```ts title="lib/sendo.ts"
import { S3Client } from "@aws-sdk/client-s3";
import { s3Storage } from "@quami/sendo/storage/s3";

export const media = s3Storage({
  client: new S3Client({
    region: "auto",
    endpoint: process.env.S3_ENDPOINT, // e.g. https://<account>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com; omit for AWS
    credentials: {
      accessKeyId: process.env.S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID!,
      secretAccessKey: process.env.S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY!,
    },
  }),
  bucket: process.env.S3_BUCKET ?? "sendo-media",
});

export const sendo = createSendo({ adapter, media /* , ... */ });
```

Keep the bucket private: the inbox only ever shows signed URLs. Some S3-compatible stores reject the CRC32 checksums recent AWS SDK versions send by default; if uploads fail with a checksum error, pass `requestChecksumCalculation: "WHEN_REQUIRED"` to the `S3Client`.

For `sendo doctor --config <module>` and `sendo mcp`, export `media` next to `adapter` from the module so doctor checks that bucket. A custom store should pass `runMediaStoreContract(name, () => store)` from `@quami/sendo/adapters/contract`.

## Transport

Graph API calls go through a `Transport`. The config shorthand builds `metaDirect` for you; build it yourself to change the Graph version or `fetch`:

```ts title="ts"
import { GRAPH_API_VERSION, createSendo, metaDirect } from "@quami/sendo";
import { memoryAdapter } from "@quami/sendo/adapters/memory";

// Same as the appSecret / verifyToken / resolveToken shorthand, plus transport options.
const transport = metaDirect({
  appSecret: process.env.SENDO_META_APP_SECRET ?? "",
  verifyToken: process.env.SENDO_VERIFY_TOKEN ?? "",
  resolveToken: (account) => process.env[account.tokenRef],
  version: GRAPH_API_VERSION, // pinned Graph API version, e.g. "v26.0"
});

export const sendo = createSendo({ adapter: memoryAdapter(), transport });
```

Any object implementing the `Transport` interface (`send`, `fetchMedia`, optional `uploadMedia`, `markRead`, `handleWebhook`, `subscribe`) can be passed as `transport`:

```ts title="ts"
import type { Account, FetchedMedia, MessagePayload, Transport } from "@quami/sendo";

// The interface metaDirect implements. Pass any object implementing it as `transport`.
export class GatewayTransport implements Transport {
  readonly kind = "gateway";

  async send(account: Account, payload: MessagePayload): Promise<{ metaMessageId: string }> {
    return gateway("send", { phoneNumberId: account.phoneNumberId, payload });
  }

  async fetchMedia(account: Account, mediaId: string): Promise<FetchedMedia> {
    return gateway("media", { phoneNumberId: account.phoneNumberId, mediaId });
  }

  // Optional: uploadMedia?(account, input), markRead?(account, metaMessageId),
  // handleWebhook?(request) → Response, subscribe?(handler) → unsubscribe.
}
```

With a transport that isn't `metaDirect`, `sendo.handleWebhook` delegates to `transport.handleWebhook` (and throws `ConfigError` when it has none), and `sendo.templates.sync()` throws `NotImplementedError`. Media uploads and `markRead` throw `NotImplementedError` when the transport doesn't implement them.

## Typed errors

Every error extends `SendoError` and carries a stable string `code`. Branch on `instanceof` or on `code`; `toJSON()` never includes `cause` or `stack`, and Meta error strings are redacted.

| Class                       | code                                                                              | Fields / thrown when                                                                                                                                                                   |
| --------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `WindowClosedError`         | `WINDOW_CLOSED`                                                                   | conversationId, expiresAt. Free-form send outside the 24-hour window.                                                                                                                  |
| `TemplateNotFoundError`     | `TEMPLATE_NOT_FOUND`                                                              | templateName, language, accountId, reason (missing \| not_approved \| inactive).                                                                                                       |
| `TemplateVariablesError`    | `TEMPLATE_VARIABLES`                                                              | templateName, expected, received.                                                                                                                                                      |
| `MetaApiError`              | `META_API_ERROR`                                                                  | status, metaCode (Meta's numeric code), subcode, fbtraceId, type, details, hint (billing_not_ready \| token_invalid \| window_closed \| rate_limited \| null); isInvalidToken for 190. |
| `AccountNotFoundError`      | `ACCOUNT_NOT_FOUND`                                                               | account, tenantId. Unknown or inactive account, another tenant's account, or none in the tenant.                                                                                       |
| `AmbiguousAccountError`     | `AMBIGUOUS_ACCOUNT`                                                               | candidates (account ids; only the tenant's when scoped), tenantId. Several numbers, no default.                                                                                        |
| `DuplicateAccountError`     | `ACCOUNT_EXISTS`                                                                  | phoneNumberId. accounts add / insert of a number connected (or disconnected in another tenant).                                                                                        |
| `AccountStateError`         | `ACCOUNT_STATE`                                                                   | accountId, state. purge of an active number, setDefault of a disconnected one.                                                                                                         |
| `MediaTooLargeError`        | `MEDIA_TOO_LARGE`                                                                 | mediaType, sizeBytes, limitBytes.                                                                                                                                                      |
| `UnsupportedMediaTypeError` | `UNSUPPORTED_MEDIA_TYPE`                                                          | mediaType, mimeType.                                                                                                                                                                   |
| `SignatureError`            | `INVALID_SIGNATURE`                                                               | Invalid webhook signature (handleWebhook answers 401 instead of throwing).                                                                                                             |
| `InvalidPhoneError`         | `INVALID_PHONE`                                                                   | input. Number can't be normalized to E.164.                                                                                                                                            |
| `PayloadValidationError`    | `INVALID_PAYLOAD`                                                                 | field, limit. A Meta message limit was exceeded (e.g. > 3 buttons).                                                                                                                    |
| `RecordNotFoundError`       | `RECORD_NOT_FOUND`                                                                | entity, id. Unknown conversation / message / event, or another tenant's.                                                                                                               |
| `ConfigError`               | `CONFIG_ERROR`                                                                    | Invalid config, missing token, agent conflicts.                                                                                                                                        |
| `NotImplementedError`       | `NOT_IMPLEMENTED`                                                                 | feature. The configured transport lacks the method: media uploads, markRead, or templates.sync on a transport that isn't metaDirect.                                                   |
| `EmbeddedSignupError`       | `SIGNUP_CODE_EXPIRED`, `META_PERMISSION_MISSING`, `PIN_CONFLICT`, `SIGNUP_FAILED` | step, metaCode, subcode, fbtraceId, details. `accounts.completeEmbeddedSignup` ([Embedded Signup](https://sendo.dev/docs/embedded-signup#errors)).                                                      |

```ts title="ts"
try {
  return await sendo.send.text(phone, "¿Seguimos con tu cita?");
} catch (error) {
  if (error instanceof WindowClosedError) {
    // Free-form text is blocked 24 h after the contact's last message: use a template.
    return sendo.send.template(phone, "recordatorio_cita", {
      language: "es",
      variables: ["Ana"],
    });
  }
  if (error instanceof TemplateNotFoundError) console.error(error.templateName, error.language);
  if (error instanceof AmbiguousAccountError)
    console.error("Pass { account }:", error.candidates);
  if (error instanceof MetaApiError) {
    console.error(error.status, error.metaCode, error.subcode, error.fbtraceId);
  }
  if (isSendoError(error)) {
    // Stable string codes, safe to branch on and to log: error.toJSON() has no cause/stack.
    console.error(error.code, error.toJSON());
  }
  throw error;
}
```

